  (:adr/body
  "# ADR-2607195800: Compose Kotoba SCRAM authentication and query providers

**Status**: accepted
**Date**: 2026-07-19

## Decision

The authenticated PostgreSQL flow composes two independently compiled Kotoba
components. `pg_scram.kotoba` owns SSLRequest, TLS, SCRAM and startup readiness;
`db_transport.kotoba` owns bounded Query framing and response parsing. The
consumer passes the opaque affine TLS handle returned by the authentication
provider to the query provider and closes it exactly once after the query.

Both providers remain guests of the same bounded native transport primitive.
Passing an opaque handle between them adds no syscall, file descriptor or
secret-export authority. The component linker uses separate explicit link
tables for the generic database provider and SCRAM provider, preventing either
provider from being required to export the other's surface.

## Evidence boundary

The local E2E performs a real TLS handshake, full SCRAM-SHA-256 exchange,
startup metadata, a PostgreSQL Simple Query and bounded CommandComplete plus
ReadyForQuery response over one channel. External PostgreSQL versions,
transactions, prepared statements, cancellation and production PKI remain
qualification work.")))
